Beth Friedman <bjf@visi.com> writes:
> I have a Valkyrie who's just finished the quest, but she had a scary
> moment in the middle of it. 
> 
> I used the "travel" command (_) to get to the stairway going up, and
> it walked her right into a pool of lava.  I thought the travel commend
> was supposed to avoid known traps.  

Note that lava isn't, in game terms, a trap; it's a terrain type.

> She managed to get out with a wand of teleportation, but lost her
> boots (water walking, I think, though not identified for sure yet) in
> the process -- they burned up.  Very annoying.
> 
> Is this a bug?  If so, is it a known bug?

Two major possibilities:

a) you're playing an older version, and ran into C342-28 "Travel
   doesn't consider water or lava when selecting a path" (supposed to
   have been fixed in 3.4.3), or
b) you started on a trap square and encountered C341-12 "If starting
   from a location with a known trap, the travel command may
   misbehave.", which is still open.

Minor possibilities would be your encountering an as-yet unlisted bug,
or the C342-28 fix not being as effective as it was supposed to be.

